From 5f3868da2af466946f716e33e8ce7ff05be5e3ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:11:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 088/101] MAS local: fit the lean window to its real size after
 a resize

When a resize by an edge or a corner ended, the guest screen was fitted
to the container's size(). Qt passes native geometry changes on to the
widget asynchronously, so when the last move and the button release are
handled together, size() is still an older size and the window jumps
back to it. The fit now uses the native window size the drag left.

The drag also follows only mouse moves with the left button down.
Windows sends moves at the real cursor whenever the window changes under
it; during a real drag that is the drag itself, but with the button up
(input sent by a tool or a test) they are not part of the drag.

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#58
Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#59

Change-Id: I8adb65ee8b0634b844d772db1e4d1577a23e156f
